scripts/ste-lint.py is copied unchanged from a later commit,
a4905d922500dd7530ca8a0eb9e4940494255709 (2026-11-11, retrieved 2026-11-12).
That version includes long-sentence word-count fixes by Yuri Perin
(https://github.com/yupasik), merged upstream as pull requests #25 and #26,
and his front-matter description, character-reference, link and list-item
fixes, merged as #50, #51, #54, #56, #62 and #63; fixes for Markdown parsing,
hedges and the --disable flag by Mathias Nielsen
(https://github.com/mathiasesn), merged as pull requests #30 to #35 and #47
to #49; code-fence and HTML-block tracking by Artur Bańkowski
(https://github.com/abankowski), merged as #40, #43 and #53; MkDocs
admonition parsing by jeevanabhi-r (https://github.com/jeevanabhi-r), merged
as #61; and list-marker and heading fixes committed upstream under the name
"t", with no pull request and no linked GitHub account.
Upstream, tim kennedy (https://github.com/tksunw) wrote the linter's first
version, and kidego5150 (https://github.com/kidego5150) and Lloyd Douglass
(https://github.com/theamericandrm) changed it later.

